 anything anywhere about a mortal ghoul being able to devour the soul of a vampire along with his blood?<br /> I'm searching but I found only something vaguely related in Thousand Years of Night ( the opposite: vampires diablerizing mortals ).<br /> <br /> The most plausible way I can think of is a Demonic Investment or pact. The objective is to steal vampire powers without dying. Any advice or idea?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think one of the possible origins of VII in 1e related to the legend of the ocurrence of one such incident, where a centuries old ghoul king consumes the torpid elder he had a sort of pact with as revenge for a betrayal by the vampire's brood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-11-2021, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T00:05:14-08:00","id":1470262,"title":"","content":"The only instance I can recall was the Cathedral of Flesh devouring Yorak being treated as diablerie in <i>Transylvania Chronicles</i>. But it was hardly an ordinary ghoul, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}